# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and on checkout, on every
# platform. Git's Windows default is core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites files to
# CRLF in the working tree; a shell script that arrives that way fails at the
# shebang on Linux with "bad interpreter ... bash^M", and the tooling here is
# developed on Windows and macOS and deployed on a Linux GPU box.
#
# Committed as a file rather than left to core.autocrlf so it holds for every
# clone, including ones nobody configured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, and never to be touched.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.onnx binary
*.spm binary
*.bin binary
